Chemical warehousing — HSE HSG71 (@cs-hsg71: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_6MKP347GP6BY1H1PCKCJKAV91R
UK Health and Safety Executive. Chemical warehousing: The storage of packaged dangerous substances, fourth edition, 2009, HSG71, ISBN 9780717662371. [Official record](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/books/hsg71.htm) · [Complete 65-page guide](https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/priced/hsg71.pdf).

Read the entire guide and reconstruct its storage, segregation, facility, emergency and continuing-review reasoning for a documented store. Use its full context when interpreting a particular table or facility measure; the operational case must identify product, quantity, packaging and jurisdiction.

The official PDF's title, contents and 2009 Crown copyright notice were inspected on 29 October 2026. The current HSE website states OGL v3 except where otherwise stated, while this dated PDF contains its own reserved-rights notice; preserve the actual component conditions rather than assigning a uniform licence. Historical legislative references need current local verification. The book remains external.

